      "title": "St. John Fisher University Portal",
      "description": "St. John Fisher University Portal | Home Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Fisher Homepage Human Resources Campus Map Thank you for your interest in employment opportunities at St. John Fisher University. We are pleased that you are considering us. St. John Fisher University is a collaborative community dedicated to teaching and learning in a personalized educational environment. The University is guided by its Catholic heritage, as expressed in the motto of its founders, the Basilian Fathers: \"teach me goodness, discipline, and knowledge. “Through an education rooted in the liberal arts, we prepare individuals for lives of intellectual, professional, and civic integrity, in which diversity and service to others are valued and practiced. NOTICE: All Librarian employment opportunities will be listed under \"Staff\" We encourage all those interested to sign up for \"Job Alerts\" in order to be automatically notified when new employment opportunities become available. Please see the menu option to the left to sign up. Students Faculty Staff Adjunct Why Fisher? Culture of Belonging About Fisher Life in Rochester Contact Us St. John Fisher University Human Resources Department Kearney Hall Room 211 3690 East Avenue Rochester, NY 14618 Phone: (585) 385-8048 Email: hr@sjfc.edu Equal Employment Opportunity It is the policy of St. John Fisher University to provide Equal Employment Opportunity to all employees and applicants for employment in accordance with the applicable federal, state, and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment in each locality in which the College has employees. The College does not discriminate against applicants or employees in hiring, promotion, termination or the terms and conditions of employment on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, perceived sex, gender identity, gender expression, the status of being transgender, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, disability, marital status, military status, veteran status, predisposing genetic, characteristics or genetic information, arrest or conviction record, status as a victim of domestic violence, or any other characteristic protected by law. The Title IX Coordinator is the designated College official with primary responsibility for coordinating compliance with Title IX and related federal and state laws. The Title IX Coordinator, Meg Flaherty, Ph.D., can be reached by phone (585-385-8232), email (titleix@sjfc.edu), in-person in Campus Center 206, or outside of business hours by contacting the Office of Safety and Security (585-385-8111). Safety and Security In accordance with the Crime Awareness and Campus Security Act of 1990 (the \"Clery Law\"), St. John Fisher University has information available for prospective students and employees on crime prevention and statistics, policies on sexual misconduct, and policies on drug/alcohol use and possession. For more information, contact the Safety and Security Department at (585) 385-8025 or the Office of Marketing and Communications at (585) 899-3801. Human Resources The Human Resources team is committed to enriching the work, teaching, and life experiences for all faculty and staff, in support of the College’s mission. Our team is dedicated to providing high quality service with a true sense of personal value for all faculty, and staff. 3690 East Avenue Rochester, New York 14618 (585) 385-8000 Back to top Copyright © St. John Fisher University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
